-- title:
--   Refinements of the Gauss ring over a supersingular place, q=2
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q=2$, a non-zero level $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ consisting exactly of the supersingular places (rational affine geometric places whose value at the geometric $j$-generator lies in the supersingular $j$-set). Assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ along $A$ with values in that residual function field, compatible with coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series over $A$. Further data: $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$; an index $\zeta$ of primitive $q$-th roots of unity; families $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$, subject to: the Laurent-ratio description of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ over $A$, transitivity of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-translates $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$ on the $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$-family, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$, permutation of the family by $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$ for any index, the condition $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s) \cap \overline{\mathbb Q} = A$, compatibility of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ with $R_0$ (elements of $R_0$'s integers that are regular wherever $\hat\jmath$ is and whose reduction is integral at $s$ lie in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, with prescribed residue given by evaluation at $s$), $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$-invariance of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ under $\Gamma_0(M')$, and existence of an element of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ all of whose translates by elements of $A$ are units. Finally let $K_0$ be a subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}/K_0$ algebraic and $\pi \in K_0$, and $A_0$ a henselian discrete valuation domain with an injective local homomorphism $\iota : A_0 \to A$ whose image is $A \cap K_0$, inducing a surjection onto $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, with maximal ideal generated by $\varpi_0$ and $\iota(\varpi_0) = \pi$; let $F_0$ be the subfield of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of those elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, assumed to contain the image $\hat\jmath$ of $jq$, and equipped with an $A_0$-algebra structure induced by $\iota$. Then for $s \in W$ and valuation subrings $V, V'$ of $F_0$ such that each is contained in the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, each omits some element of $F_0$ lying in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, and each has the property that every $g \in F_0$ integral over the $A_0$-subalgebra generated by $\hat\jmath$ whose image lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is a non-unit of it, one has $V = V'$.
--
--   This is the unibranch, or uniqueness, statement for the Igusa–Gauss component at a supersingular point in the case $q = 2$: a proper refinement of the traced Gauss ring $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty) \cap F_0$ lying over the supersingular floor place $s$ is unique. It feeds the corresponding statement for the Igusa rings on the semistable covering of the descended full-level model.
